# Docs are scratch by default (kept local). Canonical docs are explicitly
# un-ignored below; promote a doc by adding a !line and committing it.
docs/*
!docs/examples/
!docs/public/
!docs/NAMING_CONVENTIONS.md
!docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM_V2.md
!docs/WAR_PATH.md
!docs/OPERATIONS.md
!docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
!docs/contract-facts.md
!docs/decisions/
!docs/_archive/
!docs/ALIGNMENT-CATALOG.md
!docs/RISK_REGISTER.md

# docs/phases/ is published by allowlist, not wholesale: the directory is
# re-included, its contents re-excluded, and only the files that source code
# or the README actually cites are named back in. Keep this two-step —
# git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is still excluded.
!docs/phases/
docs/phases/*
!docs/phases/vault-flavors.md
!docs/phases/alignment-target-requests.md
!docs/phases/design-pass-blockers.md
!docs/phases/tier-denomination-visibility.md

